From 707cac9f6e2dee8b8225189687972f5f84adf7bd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 20:57:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] scratch archive: archive the shapes it refused
 forever (promisor tags, bare repos, linked worktrees, fifos)

worker-2 kept 54 aged scratch trees (37.8 GiB) because every retry of the
archive failed the same way (t_01a1d67a853b3b97). Now:

- unpushed detection leaves out refs whose tip the remote holds: contained in
  refs/remotes, or fetched from a promisor pack (rev-list
  --exclude-promisor-objects). Remaining refs are bundled only when every
  object is local; a ref needing promisor-vouched objects is recorded in
  promised_refs (its local objects are in the payload); objects nothing vouches
  for refuse as `unrecoverable_objects`. An empty remainder writes meta.json only.
- bare repositories bundle their refs (--all minus remotes), meta `bare: true`.
- linked worktrees/submodules: gitdir inside the tree archives as a nested repo;
  outside, worktree diff + untracked + HEAD/branch through a private index copy
  so git never writes to the outside gitdir. Missing/empty/non-dir gitdirs and
  .git symlinks still refuse.
- fifos/sockets are recorded (path, type, mode) without content; device nodes
  still refuse.

All removal guards are unchanged (terminal-owner recheck, custody fail-closed,
owned-job veto, rename fence). RED on base: 15 of 20 new tests fail.
